  },
  {
   "@id": "http://localhost:8080/how-much-does-a-moving-company-cost/#faq",
   "@type": "FAQPage",
   "mainEntity": [
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "A 2,000 sq ft house usually has about 3 bedrooms, so a local move costs $1,150–$2,850 for 10 road miles, off peak, with no stairs or add-ons. Moved 1,000 road miles, it costs $4,000–$8,550. A full basement, a packed garage or heavy furniture can push how much does a moving company cost above those ranges."
     },
     "name": "How much does a moving company cost to move a 2,000 sq ft house?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Plan for what the quote leaves out: tips, packing supplies if you pack yourself, cleaning, utility deposits, and travel or a hotel night on a long move. On an interstate move, add full-value protection if the price includes only basic released value. A cushion on top of how much does a moving company cost also covers access fees that only show up on moving day."
     },
     "name": "How much should you set aside beyond the moving company's bill?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Many local companies do, often two to four hours, and some add a trip fee for the drive to your home. On a small job the minimum can matter more than the hourly rate, because you pay for it even if the crew finishes early. Ask for the minimum and the travel policy in writing."
     },
     "name": "Do moving companies charge a minimum number of hours?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes. Many companies sell labor only: a crew loads or unloads a truck or container you rent, and you drive. It costs less than a full-service move because the company supplies no truck and no driver. The comparison on this page can add loading help to the rental-truck price, so you can set it beside a full-service crew."
     },
     "name": "Can you hire a moving company without its truck?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Not always. On a local hourly move, the final bill follows the hours the crew actually works, plus any fees for access or extra services. On an interstate move, ask whether the written estimate is binding or non-binding before you compare how much does a moving company cost from one company to the next."
     },
     "name": "Is a moving company's quote the final price?"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
